## Serve

The preview is served from the repository root on the slot's `web` port (read from
`.polier-slot`, never hard-coded):

  PORT=$(python3 -c "import json; print(json.load(open('.polier-slot'))['ports']['web'])")
  python3 -m http.server "$PORT" --bind 127.0.0.1

  curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' "http://127.0.0.1:$PORT/apps/web/preview/"        -> 200
  curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' "http://127.0.0.1:$PORT/apps/web/preview/locales/en.json" -> 200
  curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' "http://127.0.0.1:$PORT/apps/web/preview/locales/de.json" -> 200

## Browser and capture

Chrome for Testing from the Playwright cache, version 156.0.8078.4:

  "/Users/rasulatashev/Library/Caches/ms-playwright/chromium-1248/chrome-mac-arm64/Google Chrome for Testing.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome for Testing" \
    --headless=new --disable-gpu --hide-scrollbars --no-sandbox \
    --remote-debugging-port=9334 --user-data-dir=/tmp/p042-chrome-profile-2 about:blank

A temporary out-of-repo helper (`/tmp/p042-cdp.mjs`, Node built-ins only: `fetch` + the
global `WebSocket`) drove the DevTools Protocol and was removed after the run. It used
`Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride {width, height, deviceScaleFactor: 1, mobile: width < 500}`
for the exact 1440 x 900 and 390 x 844 viewports (Chrome clamps a command-line window at
mobile widths), `Emulation.setEmulatedMedia` with `prefers-color-scheme` for the system
cases, `Page.captureScreenshot`, real `Input.dispatchMouseEvent`/`Input.dispatchKeyEvent`
events, and `Page.addScriptToEvaluateOnNewDocument` to record the theme, the stored value
and the root background at the first animation frame after a reload. Colours are the
computed style values; the WCAG contrast is computed from their sRGB values (translucent
tokens are composited over the named surface first).

## Default, stored, reload and system cases (owner rule)

Rule: a stored `preview-theme` wins; without a valid stored value the page follows
`prefers-color-scheme`; dark is the final fallback. Storage was cleared before the two
default cases and the first-frame probe recorded `stored: null`.

| Case | Emulated system | Stored value | First frame `data-theme` | First frame root background | Final `aria-pressed` |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| no stored value | light | `null` | `light` | `oklch(0.966 0.006 150)` | sun `true`, moon `false` |
| no stored value | dark | `null` | `dark` | `rgb(18, 20, 18)` | moon `true`, sun `false` |
| stored light, system dark | dark | `light` | `light` | `oklch(0.966 0.006 150)` | sun `true`, moon `false` |
| stored dark, system light | light | `dark` | `dark` | `rgb(18, 20, 18)` | moon `true`, sun `false` |
| reload with stored light | dark | `light` | `light` | `oklch(0.966 0.006 150)` | sun `true`, moon `false` |

- The inline head script runs before the stylesheets; the first animation frame already has
  the resolved theme and background, so neither a light system first load nor a stored-light
  reload flashes the dark page. The dark cases stay dark.
- The light-system capture (`P0-42-light-system-desktop.png`) was taken with fresh storage
  (`localStorage.getItem("preview-theme") === null`), emulated light `prefers-color-scheme`,
  1440 x 900; `data-theme="light"`, `color-scheme: light`, sun pressed.
- A clean load logs no console error and no page exception. The browser may request
  `/favicon.ico` automatically, which is a 404 because the preview has no favicon. The rapid
  reload cycle additionally aborts in-flight icon requests (`net::ERR_CONNECTION_RESET` /
  `ERR_SOCKET_NOT_CONNECTED`); those are cancelled requests, not page errors, and a clean
  single load has none of them.

## Toggle (both languages)

- group sits below the DE/EN pill, right-aligned with it, at 1440 and 390.
- EN: group label `Theme`, buttons `Light theme` / `Dark theme`; DE: `Darstellung`,
  `Helles Design` / `Dunkles Design`. `data-label` equals the accessible name.
- `aria-pressed`: exactly one `true`, matching `data-theme`, after every click, reload and
  keyboard toggle.
- pointer, 1440: light default -> click dark -> `data-theme=dark`, stored `dark`, moon
  pressed; click light -> `data-theme=light`, stored `light`, sun pressed.
- keyboard: focus + Enter on the dark button switched light -> dark and stored `dark`;
  focus + Space on the light button switched dark -> light and stored `light`.
- language and theme are independent: DE + light and DE + dark both seen;
  `preview-theme` is the only theme key and `preview-locale` the only language key.

## Light theme and the rework findings

The page, masthead, demo board, cards, checklist, table, zone, toolbar and chips render
light; root and body background `oklch(0.966 0.006 150)` (`rgb(241, 245, 242)`), `color-scheme:
light`, no horizontal overflow at 1440 or 390 (`scrollWidth - clientWidth` 0). The first-pass
text measurements remain valid because `--fg`, `--muted`, `--accent`, `--danger` and the tones
are unchanged: `.lead` 7.31, `.eyebrow` 6.40, contents summary 16.11, open checklist entry
17.68, done checklist entry 4.64, zone title 15.23.

F1 — zone specimen title and delete icon (light-scoped):
- light: `.chrome-zone__title` and `.chrome-delete` compute `#fefffe` (`--card`) on the
  faint header `#33537b` (6 % `--fg` over `--tone-d`), **7.84:1**.
- dark: unchanged `#ffffff` on `#9cb9e0`, **2.0:1** — the pre-existing P0-35 specimen value,
  deliberately not changed by this rework.

F2 — idle teammate chip:
- with the idle classes applied, the cursor parent computes `opacity: 1`, the pointer
  `.demo-remote__pointer` computes `opacity: 0.4` and the name `.demo-remote__name` computes
  `opacity: 1`; the idle cue is now only the faded pointer.
- light name chip: `#f1f5f2` (`--bg`) on `#71500a` (`--tone-b`) = **6.69:1**; dark =
  10.25:1. The chip no longer inherits the 0.4 fade.

F3 — light control boundaries (light tokens only; dark unchanged):
- `--border-strong` 50 % over `--card` = `#8a8c8a`, **3.37:1**; over `--canvas` = `#808480`,
  **3.26:1** (unchecked checklist box border).
- `--accent-line` 70 % over `--card` = `#6d9182`, **3.46:1**; over `--canvas` = `#678c7d`,
  **3.19:1** (zone-drop outline).
- dark tokens still compute `--accent-line: rgba(143, 191, 175, 0.4)` and
  `--border-strong: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16)`, exactly the dark values.

P0-41 preservation: the rounded frames, the ten-point contents list and the dimmed done
entries are unchanged in code and style; this rework touched only colour tokens, the two
light-scoped chrome colours and the idle selector.

